(a) Gao's G
   p'(w)/3 = w**2 - 4*w + 2
   Gao G : resultant_r2 = 9*(r1**2 - 4*r1 - 2)*(r1**2 - 4*r1 + 2)**2/64
    factor r1**2 - 4*r1 - 2 (mult 1), r1 ~ -0.44948974: common roots r2 ~ [4.4494897] -> genuine (r2 != r1): [4.4494897]
    factor r1**2 - 4*r1 - 2 (mult 1), r1 ~ 4.4494897: common roots r2 ~ [-0.44948974] -> genuine (r2 != r1): [-0.44948974]
    factor r1**2 - 4*r1 + 2 (mult 2), r1 ~ 0.58578644: common roots r2 ~ [0.58578644] -> genuine (r2 != r1): []
    factor r1**2 - 4*r1 + 2 (mult 2), r1 ~ 3.4142136: common roots r2 ~ [3.4142136] -> genuine (r2 != r1): []
    genuine coincidence pairs (r1, r2) ~ [(-0.44948974, 4.4494897), (4.4494897, -0.44948974)]  count: 2
      |p(r1) - p(r2)| = 2.20e-39  |q(r1) - q(r2)| = 2.94e-39  cb = p(r1) ~ -4.0000000
      |p(r1) - p(r2)| = 1.56e-39  |q(r1) - q(r2)| = 2.80e-39  cb = p(r1) ~ -4.0000000
   exact: p(2+sqrt6) - p(2-sqrt6) = 0 ; q(2+sqrt6) - q(2-sqrt6) = 0 ; p(2+sqrt6) = -4 ; critical value q/c^2 with q(2+sqrt6) = 1/2
   so for cb = -4 (i.e. b = -4/c) two of the three critical points r = 2 +- sqrt6 of F1 on the (F2,F3)-fibre share the critical value; the third root of p = -4 is w = 2.

